Part 1: Prepare the server (SSH into your Jenkins EC2)
Step 1: Install nginx

  Step 2: Let Jenkins write to the web folder
    # Amazon Linux: web folder is /usr/share/nginx/html
     sudo chown -R jenkins:jenkins /usr/share/nginx/html
  # Ubuntu: web folder is /var/www/html
    sudo chown -R jenkins:jenkins /var/www/html

      Step 3: Add the trigger
        Under Triggers, tick Poll SCM and enter this in the Schedule box:
          H/5 * * * *

          Step 4: Add the pipeline
            Ex:- 
 pipeline {
    agent any
    stages {
        stage('Checkout') {
            steps {
                git branch: 'main', url: 'https://github.com/Gauravkyariya/jenkins-project.git'
            }
        }
        stage('Validate') {
            steps {
                sh 'test -f index.html && test -f script.js && test -f style.css'
            }
        }
        stage('Deploy') {
            steps {
                sh 'cp -r index.html script.js style.css /usr/share/nginx/html/'
            }
        }
    }
}
